Timestamp: 2026-06-08T16:10:00+05:30
Status: Force rebuild — honor sendEmail return value + true delivery status
Changes:
  - fee_snapshot.ts fireSnapshot(): the loop now reads sendEmail()'s
    return value ({ sent: boolean, reason? }) and updates the
    notification row's delivery_status accordingly:
      QUEUED → SENT  (with sent_at = NOW())  on success
      QUEUED → FAILED (with payload_json.failure_reason)  on failure
    Previously the code ignored sendEmail's return entirely:
      • recipients_sent was incremented even when SMTP returned
        smtp_not_configured / smtp_send_failed / invalid_recipient,
        so the "sent: 72" response was a lie.
      • Rows stayed at delivery_status='QUEUED' forever — every
        snapshot row in the DB (going back to May 30) is still
        QUEUED even though some were actually delivered.
    Net effect: we now have ground-truth proof of delivery for
    every recipient in every snapshot fire, the response counts are
    accurate, and any future SMTP outage will show up immediately
    in the response payload as `errors[].message = '<smtp reason>'`
    instead of looking like success.
  - INSERT also sets channel='EMAIL' (was NULL — only IN_APP rows
    had channel set), so the notifications table now distinguishes
    email-delivery rows from in-app-only rows.
  - Audit findings (no DB change shipped, just observations):
    • Only 31 fee_snapshot rows in the entire notifications table,
      all from 2026-05-30, all status='QUEUED'. Reflects the
      env-var-bug period now closed by V77+ + this V85 visibility
      improvement.
